[b]Sandbox and multiplayer configuration[/b]

Each skill uses one field containing five values in this order:

[code]Beginner / Intermediate / Advanced / Expert / Master[/code]

For example:

[code]56 / 104 / 192 / 304 / 416[/code]

Each tier accepts either a fixed page count or a range:

[code]120[/code] sets the book to exactly 120 pages.
[code]>80<240[/code] gives every newly spawned book an inclusive random value from 80 through 240.
[code]>80[/code] uses 80 as the minimum and the global maximum as the upper bound.
[code]<240[/code] uses the global minimum as the lower bound and 240 as the maximum.

[b]Skill books are not linear[/b]

The balance was created by hand using three main references:

[list=1]
[*][b]Real-world book sizes and subject complexity.[/b] Narrow practical guides are usually shorter than complete technical references.
[*][b]The point in a playthrough when a skill is normally used.[/b] Immediate survival knowledge is quicker to access, while advanced industrial knowledge requires a larger investment.
[*][b]The existing in-game book titles.[/b] Titles that imply essential guides, professional instruction, complete techniques, or comprehensive reference works influenced the relative size of each tier.[/list]

[b]Dynamic book weight[/b]

[code]Weight = 0.25 + (0.75 × pages ÷ 220)[/code]

[table=98%][tr][td][b]Example length[/b][/td][td][b]Resulting weight[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]80 pages[/td][td]0.52[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]220 pages[/td][td]1.00[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]352 pages[/td][td]1.45[/td][/tr]
[/table]

Other literature receives proportional pages and weight. Its boredom, stress, and unhappiness effects scale without a cap from spawned weight ÷ original weight, then apply as pages are read. A 0.5-weight hardcover gives half its original benefit; a paperback originally weighing 0.5 keeps its full benefit. Both behaviors have Sandbox controls.

[b]Pre-initialization API[/b]

Expansion mods can register a five-tier curve before world initialization:

[code=lua]
RealisticBookPages.registerSkill(
    "MyCustomSkill",
    { 80, ">100<180", 240, 360, 480 },
    { "MyCustomSkillAlias" }
)
[/code]

Server-side code can override a complete curve with `setPageCurve`, one tier with `setPageSpec`, or the non-canonical fallback with `setFallbackCurve`. Lua callers may pass real numbers or range strings. Call `RealisticBookPages.apply()` if an override is registered after initialization; registering before `OnInitWorld` is preferred.

